# Builder.io Code Generation Rules — Freeway

## File Structure
Place components in `src/components/{feature}/{ComponentName}.tsx`
Export components from index.ts in each feature directory

## Framework
Use React with TypeScript. Functional components only.

## Design Tokens
Import tokens from `src/tokens/colors.ts` and `src/tokens/typography.ts`
Never hardcode hex values in components — always use token references

## Styling
Use Tailwind CSS utility classes where possible
For frosted glass surfaces: apply `backdrop-blur-3xl` + `bg-white/55` + `border border-white/70`
For atmospheric backgrounds: use fixed positioned pseudo-elements, never inline styles on content elements

## Component Naming
PascalCase for components: `OpportunityCard`, `GoalChip`, `DockNav`
kebab-case for files: `opportunity-card.tsx`, `goal-chip.tsx`, `dock-nav.tsx`

## Color Usage
- Background: always cream (`bg-[#F5F2EC]`)
- Interactive elements only: pink (`#C366A2`)
- AI/system signals: lavender (`#534AB7`)
- Body text: midnight circuit (`#20175C`) at 65–70% opacity

## Typography
Font: Plus Jakarta Sans (loaded via Google Fonts)
Icons: Tabler Icons via `@tabler/icons-react`

## Animations
All transitions: `ease-in-out`
Minimum duration: 300ms for micro-interactions
Atmospheric pulses: 20–32s (use CSS `@keyframes`, not JS)

## Anti-patterns (never generate these)
- White or grey page backgrounds
- Score displays, leaderboards, progress bars with numerical %
- Hover effects on non-interactive containers
- Em dashes in copy
- "Job seeker", "applicant", "candidate", "resume" language
